description:
FOUND s513d (Opus, 2026-10-09) by the #2610 detector's first measurement: every Getopt::Long install was logged as "compiler assumed proto:@ / proto:, installed none" -- the compiler parsed with the prototype, the runtime registry (%pcl-sub-prototypes, what prototype() reads) has none.  PRE-EXISTING (s513d did not touch the registry writes for definitions).

REPRODUCER (scratch/s513d/q/gol.pl in the s513d worktree):
    use Getopt::Long;
    for my $n (qw(Configure ConfigDefaults GetOptionsFromArray)) {
      my $p = prototype("Getopt::Long::$n");
      print "$n ", (defined $p ? "[$p]" : "undef"), "\n";
    }
perl 5.40.3: Configure [@] / ConfigDefaults [] / GetOptionsFromArray [@].  PCL: undef x 3.
NOT reproduced by the same SHAPE alone: `sub f(@); sub f (@) {1}` / `sub g(); sub g() {2}` in a file (q/fwdproto.pl) and in a module (q/lib/T2961/M.pm via q/fwdmod.pl) answer perl's text.  So something else in Getopt/Long.pm routes its definitions to a lowering whose p-sub facts lack :prototype -- the first measurement to take: transpile Getopt/Long.pm with `pl2cl --module` and grep the (p-sub pl-Configure ...) facts list.

IMPACT: low (prototype() of these subs is rarely read); it does show that SOME definition path drops :prototype from the facts, which is the registry contract of ir-spec 2b.2a / task #2533.
